(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[18 1 "// The AOT's side of the runtime (PY8; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md §7, PYS13 (a); doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md"] [19 1 "// §10): arbace.python.aot translates each code object's IR into a Go function over this package, a"] [20 1 "// compiled interpreter: the instructions become Go statements calling the helpers below with their"] [21 1 "// arguments as constants, the jumps gotos, the decoding and the dispatch loop's switch gone. The"] [22 1 "// frame stays the machine's heap frame (its stack, locals, cells, PC and Lasti), so a compiled"] [23 1 "// function is run by the same loop (Thread.run) in place of step: a call of a Python function still"] [24 1 "// pushes the callee's frame (the Go stack never holds Python frames, RecursionError where CPython"] [25 1 "// raises it), an exception unwinds by the code's exception table, and a generator's or coroutine's"] [26 1 "// frame is resumed by the function's entry switch on its PC (a state machine over the heap frame)."] [27 1 "//"] [28 1 "// A compiled program registers its modules' IR (the loader's text) with their native functions in"] [29 1 "// pre-order (the code object, then its nested code objects in constant order); the loader attaches"] [30 1 "// them (ReadIR's irLoadedHook). Source compiled at run time (exec, eval, compile, an import of a module"] [31 1 "// not compiled ahead) goes to the host's compiler (PYI_AOT_COMPILER, arbace.python.aot compile-server)"] [32 1 "// and runs on the dispatch loop."] [35 41 "// AotKey(mode, source) -> the IR compiled ahead (its text or the binary IR)"] [36 41 "// the IR -> its code objects' native functions"] [40 1 "// aotLoop (PYI_AOT_LOOP set) leaves every code object to the loop: the compiled program run as pyi runs it,"] [41 1 "// the check's interpreted reference on the same runtime and its speed's baseline."] [46 1 "// AotKey is the key of a source text compiled ahead in mode (exec, eval, single): its SHA-256 in hex."] [52 1 "// AotRegister registers a module compiled ahead: key its source's (AotKey; \"\" for the main module,"] [53 1 "// which AotMain runs from its IR), ir its IR (the binary IR of irbin.go, or its text), natives its code objects' functions in pre-order."] [61 1 "// aotAttach is ReadIR's hook: the native functions of a registered IR set on its code objects."] [88 1 "// aotCompile is a compiled program's compiler (SetCompiler): a source compiled ahead, else the host's IR cache's"] [89 1 "// answer, else the host's."] [100 1 "// The host's IR cache (202b): the host's compiler (arbace.python.run/compile-source) keeps each answer it can keep in"] [101 1 "// WORK/ir-cache/KK/KEY, KEY the SHA-256 of \"MODE\\x00DIGEST\\x00SOURCE\", DIGEST its compiler's (the SHA-256 of its"] [102 1 "// sources). The compiler's script (PYI_AOT_COMPILER, bin/pyi's aot_module) names them on a line \"# ir-cache: DIR"] [103 1 "// DIGEST\"; a compiled program reads that cache itself, the answer the host would read first, so a run whose sources"] [104 1 "// at run time were all compiled before starts no host (about 0.6 s of every compiled program's start on the VM). Queue"] [105 1 "// 329: an answer's binary IR (irbin.go) is kept beside it as KEY.b, stamped with the runtime's key (the \"# ir-bin:\" line),"] [106 1 "// written by the first compiled program of that runtime that read the text and read in its place after"] [107 1 "// (PYI_AOT_BINARY_IR=0: neither)."] [111 21 "// the \"# ir-bin:\" line's runtime key: the binary IR sidecars' stamp (queue 329), \"\" none kept"] [138 2 "// the answer's binary IR (queue 329), written beside it by the first compiled program of the runtime (its stamp, the"] [139 2 "// runtime's key, first) that read its text"] [167 1 "// irBinaryCache (PYI_AOT_BINARY_IR not 0) reads and writes the IR cache's answers' binary IR beside their text."] [178 1 "// hostCompile asks the host's compiler (the command PYI_AOT_COMPILER names, started once: arbace.python.aot"] [179 1 "// compile-server) for source's IR: a request \"MODE\\tFILE\\tBYTES\\n\" and the source, an answer \"BYTES\\n\""] [180 1 "// and the compiler's text (arbace.python.run/compile-source's: the IR, SyntaxError: ..., incomplete)."] [231 1 "// AotMain is a compiled program's process: sys.argv and sys.path as bin/pyi run gives them, the"] [232 1 "// compiler of source at run time, the main module's IR run as __main__ (RunModule); the exit status."] [233 1 "// PYI_AOT_STATS names a file for the code objects run compiled and on the loop, and the host's compiles."] [234 1 "// PYI_AOT_MAIN (queue 284, the compiled launcher: bin/pyi python's sys.executable for a compiled program's children)"] [235 1 "// names another main module, run in its place: its source compiled at run time (a module compiled ahead with the"] [236 1 "// program is still run native), sys.path[0] its directory; read once and removed from the environment."] [241 4 "// the source decoded and compiled by RunModule (its coding spec's codec, the compiler of SetCompiler)"] [248 2 "// Go's collector (202b): a compiled program allocates fast and keeps little (its live heap tens of MB), so"] [249 2 "// GOGC's default of 100 collects every few tens of MB, 20-30% of a benchmark's time on the VM; 400 unless"] [250 2 "// GOGC says otherwise, under a soft limit of 2 GiB unless GOMEMLIMIT says otherwise (past it Go collects as"] [251 2 "// often as it must)"] [276 1 "// AotBadPC is a compiled function entered at a PC that is not an instruction's."] [281 1 "// The helpers of the compiled code: each is an operation of step's switch (eval.go) with its argument"] [282 1 "// a constant; the ones that may raise return the error, a call also a *pushFrame."] [480 1 "// AotToBool is to-bool (not false) and not (not true)."] [573 1 "// AotLoadAttr is load-attr of name i at instruction pc (its inline cache's, attr.go's loadAttrAt; 202b: it went"] [574 1 "// through AotExec and the registered operation)."] [584 1 "// AotLoadMethod is load-attr of name i at instruction pc when a call of the attribute with N simple arguments"] [585 1 "// follows (arbace.python.aot's method calls; queue 210, CPython's LOAD_ATTR's method variant): a Python function"] [586 1 "// found on an instance's type and not in its dict pushed with the instance after it (no bound method made), any"] [587 1 "// other attribute pushed with noSelf after it; AotCallMethod calls either."] [609 3 "// a built-in container's method (no instance dict): the method descriptor with the object, as descrGet"] [610 3 "// binds it"] [633 1 "// noSelf (&noSelf) is AotLoadMethod's mark of an attribute that is not a method to call with its instance: a"] [634 1 "// variable without an initializer (no init-order entry), not zero-sized, so its address is its own."] [641 1 "// AotCallMethod is call [N] after AotLoadMethod: the function with the instance first, else the attribute called."] [650 22 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220): the method and self, its first argument"] [655 4 "// the code that stands for C, called as C (queue 313): C_RETURN or C_RAISE after it"] [686 28 "// PyFunction_SetVectorcall's (queue 597)"] [710 1 "// AotStoreAttr is store-attr of name i at instruction pc."] [761 1 "// AotForIter is for-iter: the next item pushed (false), or at the end the iterator popped (true)."] [766 22 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [779 1 "// AotTruthy is the popped value's truth (the conditional jumps')."] [805 1 "// AotReraise is reraise at instruction i as step's OpReraise: RERAISE N (N > 0) sets the frame's reported instruction"] [806 1 "// back to the lasti N items down (f_lineno after a handler's re-raise; queue 279: it was the reraise's, a line 0)."] [821 1 "// AotCall is call [N KWNAMES] (kw the kwnames tuple's constant index, or -1): a Python function's"] [822 1 "// frame pushed (the *pushFrame returned: f.PC must be the next instruction's), a generator made, or"] [823 1 "// any other callable called."] [827 22 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [865 31 "// as OpMakeFunction (queue 205f)"] [882 19 "// PyFunction_EVENT_CREATE (queue 274)"] [887 1 "// AotExec runs instruction i of f's code as step runs it, for the operations the compiled code does not"] [888 1 "// spell out: the rarer ones of step's switch and every operation another file registers (RegisterOp)."] [889 1 "// f.PC is the next instruction's when it is called; an operation that jumps sets it."] [1010 5 "// a C callable that takes the dict itself (queue 250: ast's constructors and __replace__)"] [1032 1 "// AotPopIsNone pops the top and tells whether it is None (jump-if-none, jump-if-not-none)."] [1035 1 "// The register generator's helpers (queue 216): arbace.python.aot keeps the value stack in the compiled function's Go"] [1036 1 "// locals within a basic block, so these take their operands as arguments and return their results; the frame's stack"] [1037 1 "// holds only what was written back (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 216\")."] [1039 1 "// AotDrop truncates f's stack to n items (the compiled code took the rest into its locals, or popped them)."] [1042 23 "// a for loop's fresh generator left by break or return (queue 339)"] [1051 1 "// aotDropHeld is AotDrop while a for loop holds a fresh generator (queue 339): a dropped one f's loop held closed after"] [1052 1 "// the drop, the top first (the compiled code takes a loop's iterator into its locals only to pop it: return's swap)"] [1067 1 "// AotSpill writes the compiled code's locals back onto f's stack, in stack order."] [1075 1 "// AotStackCall is AotCallV's and AotCallMethodV's answer that the call goes the stack's way, nothing of it done yet:"] [1076 1 "// the compiled code writes its locals back and calls AotCall or AotCallMethod (a Python function not compiled, whose"] [1077 1 "// frame runFrames pushes, or directMax direct calls already nested; queue 216d)."] [1084 1 "// AotCallV is call [N KWNAMES] (kw the kwnames tuple's constant index, or -1) with the callable and its N arguments,"] [1085 1 "// xs, the compiled code's locals, callStack's cases in callStack's order (queue 216d): a compiled Python function's"] [1086 1 "// frame (a bound method's, self first in the callable's place; a class's __init__ callInit runs, the instance in it)"] [1087 1 "// run directly by runDirect and its value returned, a generator made, any other callable called; AotStackCall for a"] [1088 1 "// frame runFrames must push. xs is the call's own (Go's variadic array, never kept: copied where a callee may keep it)."] [1094 49 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220; a stack call's are callStack's)"] [1100 18 "// next(gen()) (queue 297)"] [1107 41 "// its generator stamped with the caller's instruction (queue 297)"] [1156 58 "// next(gen()) (queue 297)"] [1165 1 "// AotCallMethodV is call [N] after AotLoadMethodV, xs its two values (the function, builtin or attribute, then self or"] [1166 1 "// noSelf) and the N arguments, the compiled code's locals: AotCallMethod's cases, a compiled function run directly;"] [1167 1 "// AotStackCall as AotCallV's."] [1173 2 "// a call (queue 297's callSeq)"] [1175 46 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220): the method and self, its first argument"] [1183 30 "// the code that stands for C, called as C (queue 313)"] [1192 40 "// its generator stamped with the caller's instruction (queue 297)"] [1200 1 "// aotStacked is whether AotCallV or AotCallMethodV returns AotStackCall for callable (its events then callStack's)."] [1209 1 "// stackCall is a call of fn from compiled code the stack's way (AotStackCall): its code not compiled, or directMax direct"] [1210 1 "// calls nested; a generator's or coroutine's function never (the call only makes its object)."] [1216 1 "// callFunctionV is a call of the Python function fn with args from compiled code: its generator made, or its compiled"] [1217 1 "// frame run directly; AotStackCall, nothing done, when it goes the stack's way."] [1295 1 "// AotLoadGlobalV is